 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 666929,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">__sub__()</code> definition overloads the - operator for the code below to work?\n<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">class Pair:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;def __init__(self, x=0, y=0):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;self.x = x\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;self.y = y\n&nbsp;&nbsp;# Define __sub__()\n\np1 = Pair(10, 2)\np2 = Pair(8, 4)\np3 = p1 - p2\nprint(p3.x, p3.y)\n</pre>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1329794,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">&nbsp;&nbsp;def __sub__(self):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;return Pair(self.x - other.x, self.y - other.y)\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "- is a binary operator, so __sub__() needs two parameters."
    },
    {
     "id": 1329795,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">&nbsp;&nbsp;def __sub__(self, other):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;return self.x - other.x, self.y - other.y\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "The return statement creates a tuple, not a Pair object. p3 needs to be a Pair object for the print() call that accesses p3.x and p3.y."
    },
    {
     "id": 1329796,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">&nbsp;&nbsp;def __sub__(self, other):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;return Pair(self.x - other.x, self.y - other.y)\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "- is a binary operator, so <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">__sub__()</code> has two parameters. The parameters' <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">x</code> and <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">y</code> attributes are subtracted from each other, and the resulting values are made into a new <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">Pair</code>."
    }
   ],
